WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:17,370
Does that break up any questions or concerns for anybody?

00:00:17,370 --> 00:00:21,950
I do have a question about this Dr. Conner.

00:00:21,950 --> 00:00:29,630
I have several people in my life that are telling me, oh, we've got to go get surgery and

00:00:29,630 --> 00:00:32,330
not quite certain how to handle them.

00:00:32,330 --> 00:00:37,170
One of them specifically is in her 10th round of chemotherapy.

00:00:37,170 --> 00:00:41,730
And I just need some words of wisdom as what to say to them.

00:00:41,730 --> 00:00:46,810
I mean, I wrote down what you just said about putting in the hands of our Heavenly Father.

00:00:46,810 --> 00:00:48,370
And I totally believe that.

00:00:48,370 --> 00:00:51,770
But sometimes it gets overwhelming.

00:00:51,770 --> 00:00:59,890
They think they're being nice good to me, but it gets to the point where I'm avoiding

00:00:59,890 --> 00:01:00,890
people now.

00:01:00,890 --> 00:01:09,970
Well, I'd suggest you go and you read the book of Galatians because honestly, that has helped

00:01:09,970 --> 00:01:15,050
me a lot to deal with people that disagree with me.

00:01:15,050 --> 00:01:17,170
I just started it this morning.

00:01:17,170 --> 00:01:24,050
So the truth is, from a psychological standpoint, people want you to do what they're doing because

00:01:24,050 --> 00:01:28,040
it justifies what they're doing.

00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:32,760
And if you're doing what they're, even if they're running off of a cliff and jumping off

00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:37,560
of a cliff, as long as there's more people doing it, then they feel good about it.

00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:45,240
So and I'm not saying that what that person is doing is wrong for her or him, but when

00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:52,760
when someone is judging you, you can feel it, can't you?

00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:53,760
Oh, yes.

00:01:53,760 --> 00:01:57,280
And so make sure that you're not judging other people.

00:01:57,280 --> 00:02:02,760
Don't judge them that they're doing the wrong thing because you're going to be judged the

00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:03,760
same way.

00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:04,760
Okay.

00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:09,240
So just go, hey, whatever is right for you that you should do that.

00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:11,360
But don't judge me on what I'm doing.

00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:16,160
I really respect that or we're going to have to distance ourselves from each other a little

00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:20,280
bit during this process.

00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:21,800
There isn't anything wrong with doing that.

00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:27,640
And if that person is really a real friend, they'll, you know, apologize and they'll respect

00:02:27,640 --> 00:02:28,640
your decision.

00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:36,080
They're, if they're so insecure about their decision-making process, they're going to

00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:45,360
be more apt to pressure you to do what they're doing because that will give them more security.

00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:53,120
So it's really coming from that person's insecurity, but it still doesn't feel good.

00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:54,120
So I understand that.

00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:57,560
So you're, you're just going to, you might have to have a talk with that person if they're

00:02:57,560 --> 00:02:58,560
close.

00:02:58,560 --> 00:03:01,040
If they're a family member that you, that they're not, that they're always going to be in

00:03:01,040 --> 00:03:02,040
your life.

00:03:02,040 --> 00:03:07,400
If they're not a family member, that's going to be not in your life and you could, you know,

00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:12,400
move them, move that relationship a little, make a little distance in that relationship.

00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:14,720
It might be the best thing to do.

00:03:14,720 --> 00:03:15,720
Okay.

00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:19,820
Thank you.

00:03:19,820 --> 00:03:25,620
The biggest thing is you want to respect everybody's decision because it's their decision.

00:03:25,620 --> 00:03:33,100
And when you, when we stop judging other people, then we're not judged with that same judgment.

00:03:33,100 --> 00:03:38,220
But even when we stop judging other people, people could be judging us.

00:03:38,220 --> 00:03:43,580
And those are people that maybe we either have a talk with and say, you know, you're judging

00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:46,140
me on the decision-making.

00:03:46,140 --> 00:03:52,900
You need to respect my decision or we need to not talk so much.

00:03:53,900 --> 00:04:00,500
And if they're truly a friend and they're truly mature, then they should be able to handle

00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:01,500
that.

00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:08,340
If, if not, then, then maybe, maybe it was time to say goodbye for a while.

00:04:08,340 --> 00:04:13,220
So that, that would be by a period.

00:04:13,220 --> 00:04:14,620
So thank you.

